; dungeondelete.eval — deleting a dungeon and its levels (W10), in a scratch
; world of its own (run with -project wt_dng; WorldTest makes and removes it).
;
; EACH RULE, ONE AT A TIME, with its CONTROL: put the obstacle in place and
; demand the refusal naming it, then lift it and demand the delete is allowed
; again — so a refusal cannot be passing because something else refused.
; Then the dialog's typed confirmation (wrong case and a prefix must do
; nothing), and the console's form. WorldTest reads the files afterwards: a
; deleted level that `savemap` wrote back would be the stash rule failing.
logecho on
reset
dungeons
; The starter dungeon holds the party's level.
dungeons what keep
newtype dungeons
levels new dungeon1
dungeons
dungeons what dungeon1
; A stair from OUTSIDE leading in (room1 -> dungeon11, the next level).
stairadd stairs_down 7 7
dungeons what dungeon1
undo
dungeons what dungeon1
; A doorway on the world map leading in.
worldloc add dungeon door2 2 2
worldloc set door2 dungeon dungeon1
dungeons what dungeon1
worldloc del door2
dungeons what dungeon1
; The harness's level.
worldprops eval dungeon11
dungeons what dungeon1
worldprops eval room1
dungeons what dungeon1
; The game's opening.
worldprops opening dungeon1 dungeon11 8 8
dungeons what dungeon1
worldprops opening world
dungeons what dungeon1
; PULL dungeon11 INTO MEMORY before deleting it. The type sweep parses every
; level into a stash, and a stash left behind is exactly what `savemap` would
; write back below. Without this line that check was VACUOUS — measured: with
; the stash-forgetting line deleted from DeleteLevel, the file stayed gone,
; because nothing had ever held it.
typerefs decorations nosuch
; The type editor's Delete: the typed confirmation.
dungeons dialog dungeon1
dungeons dialog delete
dungeons dialog confirm DUNGEON1
dungeons
dungeons dialog confirm dungeon
dungeons
dungeons dialog confirm dungeon1
dungeons
levels
; Must NOT write the deleted level back.
savemap
; The console's form: the id twice, exactly.
newtype dungeons
levels new dungeon1
dungeons delete dungeon1 Dungeon1
dungeons delete dungeon1 dungeon1
dungeons
